rget_id":"176d-6bb4-df56-49cd"},{"link_uuid":"94e02518-1748-415a-bb82-d8ffe8037e19","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2e16-cd19-2323-4ae2"},{"link_uuid":"a4952deb-e294-4472-b6b4-5776aacfac3e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2d1c-9bf5-2df1-4c86"},{"link_uuid":"ba84589c-30ff-414a-840a-ced8688fb24e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"e63c-d987-6b99-4b56"},{"link_uuid":"03553efc-e0d1-4855-a0c0-1f22cc99e0df","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d064-1660-c088-4a75"},{"link_uuid":"7f3c15cc-5dd1-4f83-a8f2-f40078ed22a3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"da31-f9d1-a81d-448c"},{"link_uuid":"2e8ddcbc-b84d-4bf0-8d45-487f7a0a7a3d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"8efe-9ceb-7d89-4a33"},{"link_uuid":"183c1f70-d7d7-47de-922d-da02dc162efa","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7504-a127-e9b0-42bb"},{"link_uuid":"b7d2be33-89b5-41ca-aebf-51fcc26b484b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"723f-c5b2-d83b-43cb"},{"link_uuid":"559bab04-2431-47fd-a8fa-8420b4a04240","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3803-8e04-7c32-4b80"},{"link_uuid":"0a039548-67e4-4fe8-b35d-de6aa1c59de2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7be3-69af-6e84-4235"},{"link_uuid":"30c17e53-954c-4088-ac6d-baffb351a222","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"8537-78ba-fe3f-42d9"},{"link_uuid":"0d592826-e225-4e58-a7a8-f5ed8fa25c43","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"c9c6-a713-8bc6-4088"},{"link_uuid":"6790fc5b-72c0-4146-99fc-dc4d905201dc","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1de3-a19f-c4ea-4b28"},{"link_uuid":"67fc7427-4566-44bf-95db-f3fff67911d3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fc0c-e218-8b34-4858"}],"description":"Six subsystem agents triaged every substantial comment in `src/rebar` (439 files) against the\nmaintainer's destination taxonomy: history belongs in tickets, architecture in ADRs, logic in code,\ncontracts in schema, and comments carry only proximate just-in-time context in concise language.\n\nTotal recoverable: **~2,033 lines**. Per shard: reconciler ~970, plan_review+workflow ~230,\nstore/reducer ~230, llm core ~218, commands/CLI ~205, root/services ~180.\n\nThe largest single category is self-referential: **prose explaining the 800-LOC cap**, occupying the\nbudget it describes. 28 sites in the reconciler alone carry variants of \"RELOCATED VERBATIM out of\ntransport.py; this module changes no behaviour. The move is forced by the LOCKED 800-line cap.\" The\nloop closes at `outbound_differ.py:164`, which records that a fix had to \"buy its lines back from\nreal duplication instead of from comments\" because the module sat at the cap.\n\nHeadroom recovered where it is tightest: `runner.py` 3 → ~48 lines (the repo's #1 hotspot, 88\ncommits, whose 371-line method sits at its C901 ceiling); `_ref_lock.py` 1 → ~21; `dispatch_one.py`\n14 → ~57; `inbound_differ.py` 18 → ~66; `fetcher.py` 29 → ~80.\n\nHonest counterweight, and it must not be lost: **comment triage cannot fix three files.**\n`_store/event_append.py` (791) recovers ~10 lines; `reducer/_processors.py` (777) recovers ~3;\n`signing.py` (798) recovers ~5-8. Their comments ARE the replay-compat and security invariants. Each\nshard identified the real call-graph seam instead, and those splits are out of scope here.\n\nEvery shard produced a `do_not_move` list — blocks that look relocatable but are load-bearing. Those\nlists are the protection record and must be preserved (appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md`) so a\nfuture sweep does not re-flag them. Examples: \"on DC 8.17.1 the `fields.parent` write answers HTTP\n204 and is silently ignored. Do not 'simplify' that extra round trip away\"; \"ACLI's `--out`/`--in`\nare INVERTED relative to the naive reading\"; \"READ FROM `exc.response.headers`, NOT `exc.headers`\".\n\nVerified-stale comments found along the way (correctness, not verbosity): six sites say the\ndeterministic floor is \"P1-P9\" while `DET_CHECKS` has 11 entries and runs P1..P11; three sites in\n`llm/` assert an Anthropic constraint that `structured.py:228-238` explicitly calls \"a stale\nrationale\" and \"a relic\" 210 lines below one of them; `_backend_registry.py:3` says \"STUB:\nsignatures pinned, bodies to be implemented\" while `select_backend` is imported by 13 modules;\n`_io/__init__.py:14` says the import side \"lands in a later sub-task\" six lines above the line that\nimports it; `reducer/llm_format.py:1-28` documents a key map that omits four keys present directly\nbelow it and cites a module path that does not exist.\n\n~13 new ADRs are proposed across the shards, each consolidating an argument currently restated 4-8\ntimes. The largest: \"one idempotent transform, applied fit-then-normalize, on the local side only\" —\nthe same four-paragraph argument at 8 sites, warning that \"Swapping the two re-introduces a diff\nthat never converges.\"\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All six shards complete, each landing separately\n- [ ] Each shard's `do_not_move` list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` before that shard's edits land\n- [ ] History that already cites a ticket is reduced to the citation; history citing none has a ticket filed first\n- [ ] Proposed ADRs are written and the inline blocks reduced to citations\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected, not deleted, where they document a live invariant\n- [ ] No file's comment density is reduced by deleting a load-bearing invariant\n\n## CORRECTION (plan-review BLOCK, criteria E1/E2/F1)\n\nTwo ACs were unmeasurable: the ~2,033-line recovery headline had no covering criterion, and\n\"Proposed ADRs are written\" named no specific ADR set. Superseded below. The line-recovery\ncriterion is deliberately framed as a MEASURED-AND-RECORDED outcome, not a fixed target — this\nis the same correction the 9ce8 shard's own plan-review already blessed (\"the number is an\noutput of the work, not an input to it\"); mandating a fixed >=2,000-line floor would contradict\nthat and incentivise manufactured relocations.\n\n## Disposition vocabulary (what the ACs measure against)\n\nA **unit** is one contiguous comment block (a run of adjacent comment lines, or a single\ndocstring). Every in-scope unit gets exactly one disposition:\n\n- **RELOCATE** (non-KEEP) — the prose moves to its taxonomy destination (history -> ticket,\n  architecture -> ADR, contract -> schema) and the inline block is reduced to a one-line\n  citation. Recovered lines = block minus citation.\n- **DELETE** (non-KEEP) — redundant/obsolete prose with no destination worth keeping; removed\n  outright. Recovered lines = whole block. Only after confirming it is not load-bearing.\n- **KEEP** (KEEP-class) — proximate just-in-time context that belongs exactly where it is;\n  untouched, not counted as recovered.\n- **DO_NOT_MOVE** (KEEP-class) — looks relocatable but is load-bearing (measured external-API\n  fact, anti-refactor warning, or a lint/type-checker pragma); retained VERBATIM and recorded on\n  the shard's `do_not_move` list. Not counted as recovered.\n- **CORRECT-IN-PLACE** (KEEP-class) — a verified-stale comment documenting a LIVE invariant;\n  the text is corrected where it sits, not moved. Not counted as recovered.\n\n\"non-KEEP unit\" in the ACs = the RELOCATE and DELETE classes only. KEEP, DO_NOT_MOVE and\nCORRECT-IN-PLACE are KEEP-class: retained (corrected in place where stale) and never counted as\nrecovered lines. Completeness is verified by confirming every in-scope unit carries exactly one\nof these five labels.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [ ] All six shards complete, each landing as a separate stacked change in the dependency order\n      9ce8 -> 4fc1 -> 4b94 -> ad16 -> da4c -> ab77.\n- [ ] Each shard MEASURES and RECORDS on its own ticket the actual comment lines it recovered (by\n      diff line-count), and this parent records the net total across shards. Per the 9ce8\n      correction the ~2,033 / per-shard figures are OUTPUTS to be measured, NOT targets: no\n      relocation is manufactured to reach an estimate, and a shard recovering fewer lines than\n      estimated is not a failure provided every non-KEEP unit in scope was correctly\n      dispositioned.\n- [ ] Every ADR enumerated in the shard tickets (the new ADRs and the amendments to ADR\n      0028/0055/0031/0035) EXISTS AND IS COMMITTED before any comment that will cite it is\n      collapsed -- destination first, then the relocation. This AC is met per-shard against that\n      shard's own enumerated ADR set.\n- [ ] History that already cites a ticket is reduced to the citation; history citing none has a\n      ticket filed first.\n- [ ] Each shard's `do_not_move` list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` before that shard's\n      edits land.\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only\n      where obsolete.\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost; measured external-API facts and anti-refactor warnings\n      stay verbatim.\n- [ ] No behaviour change: the full test suite AND `make lint` / `make typecheck` pass\n      unchanged across every shard. Inline pragma comments (`# noqa`, `# type: ignore`,\n      `# ruff:`, `# tickets-boundary-ok`) and any docstring a test reads via introspection\n      are load-bearing by definition and go on every shard's `do_not_move` list -- they are\n      never treated as relocatable prose.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","managed_refs":[["depends_on","176d-6bb4-df56-49cd"],["depends_on","1de3-a19f-c4ea-4b28"],["depends_on","2d1c-9bf5-2df1-4c86"],["depends_on","2e16-cd19-2323-4ae2"],["depends_on","3803-8e04-7c32-4b80"],["depends_on","723f-c5b2-d83b-43cb"],["depends_on","7504-a127-e9b0-42bb"],["depends_on","7be3-69af-6e84-4235"],["depends_on","8537-78ba-fe3f-42d9"],["depends_on","8efe-9ceb-7d89-4a33"],["depends_on","c9c6-a713-8bc6-4088"],["depends_on","d064-1660-c088-4a75"],["depends_on","da31-f9d1-a81d-448c"],["depends_on","e63c-d987-6b99-4b56"],["depends_on","fc0c-e218-8b34-4858"],["parent","b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","parent_status_uuid":"8691a3e3-eb4c-40b7-a93e-445ad9b48921","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","ticket_type":"story","title":"Comment triage: relocate history, rationale and contracts out of src","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b6f02870-1ff0-46d0-ab2f-29eaa5876f53","089b434f-ad92-4e03-9071-47d3189b52f1","94e02518-1748-415a-bb82-d8ffe8037e19","a4952deb-e294-4472-b6b4-5776aacfac3e","ba84589c-30ff-414a-840a-ced8688fb24e","03553efc-e0d1-4855-a0c0-1f22cc99e0df","7f3c15cc-5dd1-4f83-a8f2-f40078ed22a3","2e8ddcbc-b84d-4bf0-8d45-487f7a0a7a3d","183c1f70-d7d7-47de-922d-da02dc162efa","b7d2be33-89b5-41ca-aebf-51fcc26b484b","559bab04-2431-47fd-a8fa-8420b4a04240","0a039548-67e4-4fe8-b35d-de6aa1c59de2","30c17e53-954c-4088-ac6d-baffb351a222","0d592826-e225-4e58-a7a8-f5ed8fa25c43","6790fc5b-72c0-4146-99fc-dc4d905201dc","67fc7427-4566-44bf-95db-f3fff67911d3","c273e95f-0a0a-4889-88b9-9a69b4e1cb61","9f4a3750-af70-4163-a48e-0280c7cd088c","013a0d57-b39d-47d1-a6ef-b090f32cb5d8","46becb13-e0e0-429f-883c-f8597269724e","8691a3e3-eb4c-40b7-a93e-445ad9b48921","82b1d0d5-a625-4c69-82ca-b9ebc668295a"]},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786168937349788002,"uuid":"506bf4f5-ff92-403d-88c5-946760f819d2"}